  "id": "COMPOUND:10300 - PROTEIN:1234",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Voxtalisib and Potassium channel subfamily K member 3, as it is indirectly linked through multiple targets. Voxtalisib is predicted to interact with Sodium channel protein type 11 subunit alpha, which in turn is a target of several compounds, including Amidepsine D, Fuscaxanthone C, and 1,3-Diphenylpropan-1-One. All three of these compounds are predicted to target Potassium channel subfamily K member 3, indicating a possible pathway through which Voxtalisib may influence this potassium channel. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with some variation in the strength of the evidence across the three paths. The mechanism appears to involve the modulation of potassium channel activity through the interaction with sodium channel proteins, which may play a role in cellular signaling and electrophysiological processes. While the evidence is consistent, the exact nature of the interaction and its functional implications remain areas for further investigation.",
